# Governance: Universal Testing Principles

## Core Testing Philosophy

### MANDATORY: Test-Driven Development (TDD)

**CRITICAL RULE**: Every code change MUST follow TDD approach with issue creation first.

#### 1. Issue-First TDD Workflow (MANDATORY)
1. **Create GitHub Issue**: Document requirement before any code
2. **E2E Test First**: Create end-to-end test that reflects real user flow (purpose: define acceptance criteria)
3. **Minimal Implementation**: Implement only what makes the E2E test pass (purpose: avoid over-engineering)
4. **Unit Test Coverage**: Add unit tests for reusable logic (purpose: ensure code reliability)
5. **Test Maintenance**: Update existing tests for changed behavior (purpose: maintain test integrity)

#### 2. TDD Enforcement Rules
- **No Code Without Test**: Never write implementation code without a failing test first
- **Red-Green-Refactor**: Follow the classic TDD cycle strictly
- **Test Defines Requirements**: Let tests drive the implementation design
- **Minimal Implementation**: Only implement what's needed to make tests pass

### Testing Hierarchy
- **E2E Tests**: Validate complete user workflows (MUST be written first)
- **Integration Tests**: Test component interactions
- **Unit Tests**: Test individual functions and methods
- **Regression Tests**: Ensure existing functionality remains intact

## Test Organization

### Test Structure
- Use isolated test directories to prevent interference
- Follow consistent naming conventions
- Organize tests by functionality and scope
- Maintain clear test descriptions

### Test Execution
- Run tests in isolation to prevent side effects
- Use cleanup procedures to maintain clean state
- Execute tests in predictable order
- Capture and report test results consistently

### Test Artifacts
- Generate comprehensive test reports
- Log test execution details
- Preserve test outputs for analysis
- Clean up test artifacts after completion

## Quality Standards

### Test Reliability
- Tests must be deterministic and repeatable
- Avoid flaky tests and race conditions
- Use proper setup and teardown procedures
- Handle external dependencies appropriately

### Test Coverage
- Aim for comprehensive coverage of critical paths
- Focus on business logic and edge cases
- Test error conditions and failure scenarios
- Validate both positive and negative test cases

### Test Performance
- Keep tests fast and efficient
- Use parallel execution where appropriate
- Minimize external dependencies
- Cache test data when possible

## Testing Workflow

### MANDATORY: TDD Development Process

#### 1. Issue Creation Phase
- Create GitHub issue with detailed requirements
- Define acceptance criteria clearly
- Plan implementation approach

#### 2. Test Creation Phase
- Write E2E test that defines user flow
- Ensure test fails initially (red phase)
- Define clear acceptance criteria in test

#### 3. Implementation Phase
- Write minimal code to make test pass (green phase)
- Focus only on making the test pass
- Avoid over-engineering

#### 4. Refactoring Phase
- Clean up code while keeping tests passing
- Improve design without changing behavior
- Add unit tests for reusable logic

#### 5. Validation Phase
- Run full test suite to ensure no regressions
- Verify all acceptance criteria are met
- Document any changes made

### Local Development
1. **Quick Test**: Run individual test files for rapid iteration
2. **Full Test**: Run complete test suite for comprehensive validation
3. **Specific Test**: Use targeted test execution for focused validation
4. **Clean Test**: Use cleanup to ensure clean test environment

### Continuous Integration
1. **Automated Testing**: Run tests on every code change
2. **Cross-Platform**: Test across different environments
3. **Artifact Collection**: Capture test outputs and reports
4. **Status Reporting**: Provide clear pass/fail indicators

### Regression Testing
- **Base Tests**: Always run to ensure core functionality remains intact
- **Progressive Testing**: Each new feature adds its tests to the regression suite
- **Full Suite Execution**: Run comprehensive testing for all changes
- **Isolated Testing**: Use specific test execution for targeted validation

## Test Maintenance

### MANDATORY: Test Updates for Feature Changes

**CRITICAL RULE**: Tests MUST be updated whenever features are added, modified, or enhanced.

#### When to Update Tests (MANDATORY)
- ✅ **New features added** - Add E2E tests covering the new functionality
- ✅ **Feature enhancements** - Update existing tests to cover new behavior
- ✅ **Behavior changes** - Update tests to reflect new behavior
- ✅ **UI/UX improvements** - Add tests for new interactions (hover, preview, animations)
- ✅ **Bug fixes** - Add tests to prevent regression
- ✅ **Performance improvements** - Update tests if behavior changes
- ✅ **Accessibility improvements** - Add tests for new accessibility features

#### Test Update Requirements
1. **E2E Tests First**: Always add/update E2E tests for user-facing features
2. **Coverage**: Ensure all new functionality is covered by tests
3. **Regression**: Update existing tests if behavior changes
4. **Documentation**: Update test descriptions to reflect new functionality
5. **Showcase Integration**: Use showcase examples in tests (not mock data)

#### Test Update Workflow
1. **Identify Changes**: List all features/behaviors that changed
2. **Update Tests**: Add new tests or modify existing ones
3. **Run Tests**: Verify all tests pass with new functionality
4. **Review Coverage**: Ensure no functionality is untested
5. **Commit Together**: Commit test updates with feature code

### Test Updates
- Update tests when functionality changes
- Maintain test relevance and accuracy
- Remove obsolete or redundant tests
- Refactor tests for better maintainability

### Test Documentation
- Document test purpose and scope
- Explain complex test scenarios
- Provide setup and execution instructions
- Keep test documentation current

### Test Review
- Review tests for completeness and accuracy
- Validate test coverage and effectiveness
- Ensure tests follow established patterns
- Identify opportunities for improvement

## TDD Best Practices

### Test Writing Guidelines
- Write tests that reflect real user behavior
- Focus on behavior, not implementation details
- Keep tests simple and readable
- Use descriptive test names

### Implementation Guidelines
- Write the simplest code that makes tests pass
- Don't add features not covered by tests
- Refactor frequently to improve design
- Keep implementation focused and minimal

### Quality Assurance
- Ensure all tests pass before committing
- Run full test suite after any changes
- Maintain test coverage metrics
- Review test quality regularly

## CMS Access and Deployment

### CMS Login Credentials

**MANDATORY**: When accessing the CMS and encountering a login form, use the default credentials:

- **Username**: `wsadmin`
- **Password**: `wsadmin`

**Usage:**
- Browser access: Navigate to CMS URL and login with above credentials
- E2E Tests: Credentials are configured in `tests/end-to-end/cypress.env.json` or environment variables
- Manual Testing: Use these credentials when manually verifying showcase pages

### Deployment Workflow

**CRITICAL**: Different deployment commands for different content types.

#### 1. Application Code Deployment

**When to use**: After modifying application code (Java, HTL templates, JavaScript, CSS, clientlibs)

**Command:**
```powershell
.\deploy-app.ps1
```

**What it deploys:**
- Java Sling Models and services
- HTL templates (`.html` files)
- JavaScript files (`clientlibs/`)
- CSS files (`clientlibs/`)
- Client library configurations
- Component definitions (`.content.json`)

**Location**: `application/backend/src/main/resources/`

#### 2. Content/Showcase Deployment

**When to use**: After modifying showcase content (`.content.xml` files in `tests/content/`)

**Command:**
```powershell
.\deploy-content-tests.ps1
```

**What it deploys:**
- Showcase page content (`.content.xml` files)
- Test content structure
- Component examples and configurations

**Location**: `tests/content/src/main/content/jcr_root/content/typerefinery-showcase/`

**MANDATORY**: Always deploy showcase content after updating showcase examples to ensure E2E tests run against latest content.

### Deployment Workflow for Component Changes

**Complete workflow when updating components:**

1. **Update Application Code** (if needed):
   - Modify Sling Models, templates, JavaScript, CSS
   - Run `.\deploy-app.ps1` to deploy application changes

2. **Update Showcase Content** (if needed):
   - Modify showcase `.content.xml` files
   - Run `.\deploy-content-tests.ps1` to deploy showcase changes

3. **Verify Changes**:
   - Navigate to showcase page in browser
   - Login with `wsadmin` / `wsadmin` if prompted
   - Verify component displays correctly

4. **Run E2E Tests**:
   - Tests should run against deployed showcase pages
   - Ensure both preview and author tests pass

## E2E Testing with Showcase Pages

### Showcase Page Structure

**Location**: `tests/content/src/main/content/jcr_root/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}/`

### URL Construction for Showcase Pages

**CRITICAL**: Understanding how to construct full URLs for preview and author modes.

#### Base URLs

**For Cypress E2E Tests:**
- Base URL: `http://localhost:8113` (configured in `cypress.config.ts`)
- Cypress automatically prepends baseUrl to relative paths in `cy.visit()`

**For Browser/Manual Access:**
- Base URL: `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101`
- Use full URL construction in browser address bar

#### URL Patterns

**Preview Mode (User-facing):**
- **Pattern**: `{baseUrl}/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html`
- **Cypress**: `cy.visit('/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html')`
- **Browser**: `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html`

**Author Mode (Editing):**
- **Pattern**: `{baseUrl}/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor`
- **Cypress**: `cy.visit('/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor')`
- **Browser**: `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor`

**Key Components:**
- `/content/` - Content repository path
- `/apps/websight/index.html` - WebSight editor application
- `::editor` - Editor mode suffix (only for author mode)
- `{component}` - Component name (e.g., `input`, `button`, `checkbox`)

#### Examples

**Input Component:**
- Preview (Cypress): `cy.visit('/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/input.html')`
- Preview (Browser): `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/input.html`
- Author (Cypress): `cy.visit('/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/input::editor')`
- Author (Browser): `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/input::editor`

**Button Component:**
- Preview (Cypress): `cy.visit('/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/button.html')`
- Preview (Browser): `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/button.html`

### Writing E2E Tests for Showcase Pages

**MANDATORY**: All form components MUST have E2E tests that validate showcase page functionality.

#### Test File Structure

**Location**: `tests/end-to-end/tests/components/forms/{component}/`

**Required Test Files:**
1. **`{component}-preview.cy.ts`** - Preview mode tests (user-facing functionality)
2. **`{component}-author.cy.ts`** - Author mode tests (editing/dialog functionality)

**Example Structure:**
```
tests/end-to-end/tests/components/forms/input/
├── rating-preview.cy.ts    # Preview mode tests
└── rating-author.cy.ts     # Author mode tests
```

#### Preview Mode Tests

**Purpose**: Test user-facing functionality on showcase pages.

**Test Pattern:**
```typescript
describe('Component - Preview', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    cy.login(); // Uses wsadmin/wsadmin credentials
  });

  it('renders component correctly in preview mode', () => {
    cy.visit('/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html');
    // Test assertions
  });
});
```

**What to Test:**
- Component renders correctly
- Visual elements display properly
- User interactions work (clicks, inputs, etc.)
- Component behavior matches specifications
- Edge cases and different configurations
- Integration with form system

#### Author Mode Tests

**Purpose**: Test editing functionality and dialog configuration.

**Test Pattern:**
```typescript
describe('Component - Author', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    cy.login();
  });

  it('has editable dialog in author mode', () => {
    cy.visit('/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor');
    // Test dialog interactions
  });
});
```

**What to Test:**
- Component overlay appears
- Dialog opens correctly
- All dialog tabs are accessible
- Configuration fields work
- Changes save correctly
- Conditional fields show/hide appropriately

### Test Commands and Utilities

**Available Cypress Commands:**
- `cy.login()` - Authenticates with CMS (uses `wsadmin`/`wsadmin`)
- `cy.getByTestId(testId)` - Find element by `data-testid` attribute
- `cy.findByTestId(testId)` - Find element within subject by `data-testid`
- `cy.percySnapshotPreview(name)` - Take visual snapshot in preview mode
- `cy.percySnapshotPageEditor(name)` - Take visual snapshot in editor mode
- `cy.percySnapshotDialog(name)` - Take visual snapshot of dialog

**Test Constants:**
- Import from `support/const.ts`:
  - `selectors` - Common CSS selectors
  - `testIds` - Common test ID constants

### Verifying Pages Work

**Manual Verification Process:**

1. **Deploy Content** (if showcase was updated):
   ```powershell
   .\deploy-content-tests.ps1
   ```

2. **Deploy Application** (if code was updated):
   ```powershell
   .\deploy-app.ps1
   ```

3. **Navigate to Showcase Page**:
   - **Preview Mode**: `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html`
     - Pattern: `{baseUrl}/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}.html`
   - **Author Mode**: `https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor`
     - Pattern: `{baseUrl}/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor`

4. **Login if Prompted**:
   - Username: `wsadmin`
   - Password: `wsadmin`

5. **Verify Component**:
   - Check visual rendering
   - Test interactions
   - Verify console for errors
   - Check network requests

6. **Run E2E Tests**:
   ```bash
   cd tests/end-to-end
   npm run dev  # Interactive mode
   # or
   npm run test # Headless mode
   ```

### Testing Checklist

**Before Committing Component Changes:**

- [ ] Application code deployed (`.\deploy-app.ps1`)
- [ ] Showcase content deployed (`.\deploy-content-tests.ps1`)
- [ ] Preview page verified manually
- [ ] Author page verified manually
- [ ] E2E preview tests written and passing
- [ ] E2E author tests written and passing
- [ ] All test cases cover component functionality
- [ ] Edge cases tested
- [ ] Console shows no errors
- [ ] Component works in different configurations
